    "result_text": "Done. There's exactly one test class, and the suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec asked for an **immutable structured event** emitted via the `AUDIT` logger, in addition to the existing human-readable audit line, carrying `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}` \u2014 with the identifier field being the owner's *current primary identifier*, designed so it becomes `memberId` once customerCode is unified.\n\n**New file \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`)\n- An immutable `record` (seq, ownerId, identifier, membershipLevel).\n- `toJson()` renders the compact, deterministic object `{\"seq\":..,\"ownerId\":..,\"customerCode\":..,\"membershipLevel\":..,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` with proper string escaping and null handling.\n- The identifier is rendered under a single `IDENTIFIER_KEY` constant (`customerCode` today), so the wire shape follows the identity when it later moves to `memberId`.\n\n**`AuditOwnerCreated.java`**\n- Added a static `AtomicLong SEQ` \u2014 monotonically increasing across all creates (each create runs this step exactly once, and the counter is process-wide, unaffected by per-test transaction rollback).\n- After the existing audit line, it builds the event using `MembershipLevel.effective(owner)` (the persisted household-capped level) and a `primaryIdentifier(owner)` helper \u2014 the single seam that changes when customerCode becomes memberId \u2014 then logs `event.toJson()`.\n\nThe observed AUDIT output:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
